{
  "name": "How to Optimize Your Website for AI Visibility",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Prioritize Audiences, Services, & Questions",
      "text": "Before you change anything, identify your key customer segments, the services they care about most, and the exact questions they're asking. This isn't just guesswork; use tools like Google Search Console to find real 'unanswered questions' related to your business. This focus ensures your optimization efforts target content AI is actually looking for.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Enhance Technical Accessibility & Page Experience",
      "text": "AI crawlers need to get to your content easily. Ensure your website loads fast, is mobile-friendly, and that there are no technical barriers like misconfigured robots.txt files blocking access to important pages. Clean, low-latency HTML is preferred. Also, make sure all your core content is accessible without relying heavily on JavaScript rendering, which can be a hurdle for some AI bots.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Structure Content for Direct Answers & Facts",
      "text": "AI loves direct answers. Organize your pages so that key information, facts, and answers to common questions are immediately apparent and concise. Avoid burying critical details in long paragraphs. Use clear headings and bullet points. If you have claims, support them with first-hand details or reliable sources. This makes your content easily digestible and extractable for AI.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Implement Accurate Structured Data (Schema)",
      "text": "While not strictly 'required' by Google for its AI features, well-implemented JSON-LD structured data (like `FAQPage`, `Article`, `Service`) is incredibly helpful. It tells AI exactly what your content is about. Crucially, your schema *must* accurately represent the visible content on the page. Inaccurate or irrelevant schema can do more harm than good.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Monitor, Update, and Maintain Consistency",
      "text": "AI visibility is continuous. Monitor how AI systems are interacting with your site (if data is available) and regularly update your content. Review high-value pages after any service changes, and ensure contact information is always current. Compare performance over time, rather than relying on a single test. This ongoing effort ensures your business remains a trusted source for AI.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
